\chapter{Exceptions}
\chaplabel{exceptions}

\note{Methods and fields of exceptions, chained exceptions,
and static checking of checked exceptions are not yet supported.

Fortress examples in this chapter are not run by the interpreter.}

Exceptions are values that can be thrown and caught, via \KWD{throw}
\section{Information of Exceptions}
\seclabel{chained-exceptions}

Every exception has optional fields: a message and a chained exception.
These fields are default to
\EXP{\TYP{Nothing}\llbracket\TYP{String}\rrbracket} and
\EXP{\TYP{Nothing}\llbracket\TYP{Exception}\rrbracket} as follows:
%trait Exception comprises { CheckedException, UncheckedException }
%  getter message(): Maybe[\String\] = Nothing[\String\]
%  setter message(Maybe[\String\]):()
%  getter chain(): Maybe[\Exception\] = Nothing[\Exception\]
%  setter chain(Maybe[\Exception)\]:()
%  printStackTrace(): ()
%end
\begin{Fortress}
\(\KWD{trait} \TYP{Exception} \KWD{comprises} \{\,\TYP{CheckedException}, \TYP{UncheckedException}\,\}\)\\
{\tt~~}\pushtabs\=\+\(  \KWD{getter} \VAR{message}()\COLON \TYP{Maybe}\llbracket\TYP{String}\rrbracket = \TYP{Nothing}\llbracket\TYP{String}\rrbracket\)\\
\(  \KWD{setter} \VAR{message}(\TYP{Maybe}\llbracket\TYP{String}\rrbracket)\COLONOP()\)\\
\(  \KWD{getter} \VAR{chain}()\COLON \TYP{Maybe}\llbracket\TYP{Exception}\rrbracket = \TYP{Nothing}\llbracket\TYP{Exception}\rrbracket\)\\
\(  \KWD{setter} \VAR{chain}(\TYP{Maybe}\llbracket\TYP{Exception}\rrbracket)\COLONOP()\)\\
\(  \VAR{printStackTrace}()\COLON ()\)\-\\\poptabs
\(\KWD{end}\)
\end{Fortress}
where an optional value \VAR{v} of type \EXP{\TYP{Maybe}\llbracket{}T\rrbracket}
is either \EXP{\TYP{Nothing}\llbracket{}T\rrbracket} or
\EXP{\TYP{Just}(v)}.
\revision{revival-nothing}{The Working Draft of February 2011 wrote both
defaults as a bare \TYP{Nothing}, one object for every instantiation of
\TYP{Maybe}, which instantiation exclusion forbids
(\secref{convenience-types}).}

